        "cp`, an MCP server with a checker, fixes, the formatter, a sandboxed interpreter, the C generator, and the\n  embedded specification;\n- `llms.txt`, `llms-full.txt` and an agent guide whose ten common mistakes are compiled by `SiteTests`.\n\n**C9b is complete** (2026-10-26; `cosmoos/c9-report.md`). CosmoOS's GPT parser and writer are Nova in CosmoOS itself:\n`kernel/block/gpt.c` is novac's generated C (stage S1, checked in, written then by `c9/vendor.py`), with Nova's runtime and\na panic hook per environment. Local checks on both arches (host-test, fuzz, analyze, debug and release boots with\n`blk-gpt`) and CosmoOS's CI (47 of 47) passed; the owner merged it (`68925d14`).\n\n**novac 0.1.0 is released** (2026-10-26; `docs/release.md`): NativeAOT binaries for Linux, macOS and Windows on x64 and ARM, the macOS ones signed and notarized, installed by `site/public/install.sh` and `install.ps1` (https://github.com/vkuttyp/Nova/releases/tag/v0.1.0). `main` is `0.2.0-dev`.\n\n**CosmoOS A5, PR 1 is built** (2026-10-26; `cosmoos/a5-report.md`). The first CosmoOS feature written in Nova rather\nthan ported: `kernel/process/cputime.c` is novac's C for `cputime.nova` (the tick's\nuser/system sample, `ITIMER_VIRTUAL`/`ITIMER_PROF`, the exact user/system split), with the process side in C. Its\ntest (`lxtest`) failed 27 checks on the unchanged kernel first; host-test, fuzz, analyze and debug and release boots\npass on both arches.\n\n**The CosmoOS Nova sources moved into CosmoOS** (2026-10-27; `cosmoos/build-integration.md` §3.1), at the owner's\nchoice, folded into A5's first PR (#461): each `NAME.nova` beside its generated `NAME.c`, `make nova` with a pinned\nnovac (0.1.1), and a CosmoOS CI job that fails on drift. `integrations/cosmoos/vendor.py` is gone; `c9.py` and\n`benchmarks/gpt` read the sources from a CosmoOS checkout, and `benchmarks/gpt` now takes the C original from\n`dc1d5166` (run after C9b, it would have compared the generated C with itself; its published